": \"A safety-critical actuator gate should default to the off state, so its default bias should be a pull-down to GND, as on the ATO valve path.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R5 /GPUMP +3V3 10k\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R12 0 /GATO 10k\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"R5\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"While the ESP32 pin is floating or undriven, for example during boot or reset, the pump gate is held high. The 24 V circulation pump may run unintentionally until firmware drives the gate low through T1.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"U1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"U1.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The TPS62933 enable pin (EN, pad 2) is flagged as a no-connect and is not tied to VIN or to any control net.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The TPS62933 EN pin should be defined by a resistor divider from VIN or by a driven control signal, not left floating.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"136\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(pin (num \\\"2\\\") (name \\\"EN\\\") (type \\\"input\\\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The 24 V to 5 V buck may start or stop unpredictably, or fail to start, depending on the EN pin's internal default. That would leave the ESP32 and the 3.3 V rail unpowered.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"R29 is labelled and sourced as a 10.7 k\u03a9 part but is entered as 10.7 M\u03a9 in the Nutrient-B VREF divider, which would drive the TMC2209 current reference to full scale, a clear and high-confidence deviation. Two lower-confidence items are the pump gate pulled up to 3.3 V and the buck regulator's EN pin left floating.\"\n}",
